  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a black-and-white photo of three women performing music on stage, with text overlaid that reads 'only 30's kids will remember this.' The overall intent is to evoke nostalgia and imply that the depicted scene or music is a cultural artifact from a specific past era, likely targeting individuals who are now in their 30s. The meme is not inherently abusive, cyberbullying, hateful, misogynistic, or propagandistic. However, it can be considered harmful because it may unintentionally exclude or marginalize people who are not part of the targeted demographic (those in their 30s) by suggesting that their experiences or memories are somehow less valid or less 'authentic' than those of the group being referenced. This can foster a sense of generational exclusion or cultural elitism, which may cause emotional discomfort or alienation for those outside the specified age group. The meme relies on generational nostalgia and potentially creates a hierarchy of cultural memory, which can be exclusionary and diminish the value of experiences from other age groups.",
